## Positioning

The Flow suite is for drawing a sequence of operations as a diagram you can read and rearrange. **Flowchart** is the canvas: a dot grid, absolutely-positioned nodes, bezier connectors recomputed from measured card heights, and optional dragging with grid snapping. It deliberately owns only three things — the canvas, the connectors and the category chip — while card content comes from the host through a slot, so the same canvas can draw an automation rule, an agent's tool-call chain, or a deploy pipeline. It imports through the `@talex-touch/tuffex/ai` entry: suites are a **docs-level** split, while the component barrels stay base / pro / ai.

